§ `s 5: corruption`

#ASSERT `an offence under section 5(a) is made out` f5recv gMoney FALSE
#ASSERT `an offence under section 5(a) is made out` f5recvPb gOffice FALSE
#ASSERT `an offence under section 5(b) is made out` f5give gMoney FALSE
#ASSERT `an offence under section 5(b) is made out` f5givePb gService FALSE
-- not corrupt, no presumption
#ASSERT NOT (`an offence under section 5(a) is made out` f5recvNotCorrupt gMoney FALSE)
-- presumption supplies corruptness
#ASSERT `an offence under section 5(a) is made out` f5recvNotCorrupt gMoney (`the presumption of section 8 operates` pDirect agNone)
#ASSERT NOT (`an offence under section 5(a) is made out` f5recvNoPurpose gMoney FALSE)
-- not a gratification
#ASSERT NOT (`an offence under section 5(a) is made out` f5recv gNone FALSE)
-- giver is not within 5(a)
#ASSERT NOT (`an offence under section 5(a) is made out` f5give gMoney FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`an offence under section 5(b) is made out` f5recv gMoney FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`an offence under section 5(b) is made out` f5noAct gMoney FALSE)
#ASSERT `an offence under section 5(b) is made out` f5giveNotCorrupt gMoney (`the presumption of section 8 operates` pDirect agNone)
-- presumption rebutted
#ASSERT NOT (`an offence under section 5(a) is made out` f5recvNotCorrupt gMoney (`the presumption of section 8 operates` pContrary agNone))
GIVETH A `Section 6 Facts`
f6a MEANS
    `Section 6 Facts` WITH
        `the agent accepted or obtained, or agreed to accept or attempted to obtain, from any person, a gratification for himself or herself or for any other person` IS TRUE
        `the accused gave, agreed to give or offered a gratification to an agent` IS FALSE
        `the accused acted corruptly` IS TRUE
        `the gratification was an inducement or reward for doing or forbearing to do, or for having done or forborne to do, an act in relation to the principal's affairs or business, or for showing or forbearing to show favour or disfavour to any person in relation to the principal's affairs or business` IS TRUE
        `the accused knowingly gave an agent a receipt, account or other document` IS FALSE
        `the accused, being an agent, knowingly used with intent to deceive the principal a receipt, account or other document` IS FALSE
        `the principal is interested in the document` IS FALSE
        `the document contains a statement which is false or erroneous or defective in a material particular` IS FALSE
        `the statement is, to the accused's knowledge, intended to mislead the principal` IS FALSE

